3. Yet, these fortresses were packed with clever defensive features, including ishi otoshi mado (stone-dropping windows) designed to crush incoming attackers. (22 words)
4. Castles eventually transitioned into symbols of political power during the peaceful Edo period, rather than acting as active battlegrounds. (20 words)
5. Hundreds of years of stability followed under the shoguns, allowing arts, poetry, and bustling city culture to flourish. (18 words)
6. Even the most fearsome warriors began trading their battlefield armor for tea ceremonies and bureaucratic duties. (17 words)
7. Eventually, the arrival of the modern era swept away the old feudal system and the samurai class with it. (16 words)
8. Still, when you stand before the surviving stone walls today, they seem to whisper thrilling tales of the past. (18 words)
9. Every wooden beam and silent moat serves as a lasting bridge to that legendary time. (15 words)

